## 3.3 Progress interface

Show honest progress stages:

- Validating target.
- Checking DNS.
- Checking HTTPS.
- Measuring response.
- Inspecting security headers.
- Parsing frontend.
- Analysing linked pages.
- Checking accessibility signals.
- Measuring performance.
- Evaluating content.
- Processing evidence.
- Preparing report.

Progress must come from actual job state.

Never fabricate a completed percentage.

## 3.4 Safe scanner networking

This is compulsory.

Implement strict Server-Side Request Forgery protection.

Requirements:

- Only HTTP and HTTPS.
- Restrict normal checks to approved web ports.
- Block localhost.
- Block private IPv4.
- Block private IPv6.
- Block loopback.
- Block link-local.
- Block cloud metadata services.
- Block reserved destinations.
- Validate DNS resolutions.
- Recheck resolved IP addresses.
- Validate every redirect destination.
- Prevent DNS rebinding.
- Limit redirects.
- Apply connection timeouts.
- Apply response timeouts.
- Limit downloaded data.
- Limit concurrent requests.
- Limit crawl depth.
- Limit total requests.
- Avoid unbounded downloads.

Never forward browser authentication cookies to a scanned website.

Never forward OriginSec secrets or Firebase tokens to a target.

Never perform destructive checks against external websites.

Never perform brute-force operations, credential guessing, exploitation, denial-of-service testing, or authentication bypass attempts.

Only perform authorized, non-destructive defensive assessment.

